sub:Head {
    sub: a np:Nanopublication ;
        np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
        np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
        np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Daphnia magna ocellus-pigment Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, detail scale) faithfully reproduces Daphnia magna morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Daphnia magna specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/daphnia_magna_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Daphnia magna; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, note scipy 1.18 and Pillow 13 installed for this run; no virtualenv; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects λ_c = 2π/k_c. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies du/dt = a − u + u²v and dv/dt = b − u²v. | Macagno (1981), Smith & Macagno (1990), and Hebert & Emery (1990) are the Daphnia sources for visual-system pattern formation, ommatidial photoreceptors, and inducible cuticular melanin. None of them reports a 2.736 µm stripe period.; reconstructed_in_script: Length unit fixed so the analytical wavelength is 2.736 µm, with a = 0.062, b = 1.180, D_u = 0.016, D_v = 0.640. | Pass 2 scores σ(k) on the odd modes of the band σ > -0.15 separately from the full band. Both exceed r = 0.98. | The ratio of the saturated Fourier peak to 2.736 µm is reported as coarsening, not as a second target wavelength.; transfer_boundary: Age does not change along this 1/1 chronoseries. The melanosome and ommatidium comparisons are scale comparisons. | The 20.17 µm cuticle peak does not transfer to the 2.736 µm field, and the 2.736 µm field does not transfer to the polygons.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published 2.736 µm measurement. | Does not claim the ×130 polygons are the Turing pattern. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent, and no signature was fabricated. | Does not claim a second independent assessor.]; phenomenon_size: 2.9 µm (2.904e-06 m, log10=-5.537 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 2.9 µm to 4.6 mm): 2.9 µm:daphnia-magna-bioelectric-polarity, 5.4 µm:daphnia-magna-vertex-packing, 103 µm:daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength, 190 µm:daphnia-magna-clock-wavefront, 616 µm:daphnia-magna-morphogen-condensation, 802 µm:daphnia-magna-flux-canalization, 845 µm:daphnia-magna-elastic-buckling, 1.1 mm:daphnia-magna-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00240009>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1523/jneurosci.01-09-00945.1981>,
            <https://doi.org/10.2307/2389739> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-daphnia-magna-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

